{%- liquid
  assign sub_heading = section.settings.heading
  assign sub_intro = section.settings.subheading

  comment
    Liquid's page_title returns the SEO title whenever one is set, not the
    resource's own title. The houses now carry keyword-led SEO titles
    ("Pink Salt Scrubs & Skincare Pakistan — HALORA") that belong in the
    browser tab and in Google, not on the page — so the visible <h1> takes
    collection.title instead, and the brand naming ("Wellness · Skincare")
    is preserved. page_title stays the fallback everywhere else.
  endcomment
  assign display_title = page_title
  if template.name == 'collection' and collection.title != blank
    assign display_title = collection.title
  endif

  comment
    Collection pages used to render title -> filter bar -> grid with no
    context at all. The description was never missing: all four houses
    already have one in the admin (Collections -> [house] -> Description),
    nothing was printing it. Fall back to it whenever this section has no
    explicit subheading of its own.

    Keep house descriptions to a single paragraph. The outer <p> is
    stripped so the text lands as a direct child of .halora-subhero, which
    is what the CSS styles (".halora-subhero > p"). Inline markup such as
    <em> or a link survives; a second paragraph would be merged into the
    first rather than breaking the layout.

    /collections/all is Shopify's virtual route - no Collection record, so
    page_title is the literal string "Products" and collection.description
    is empty. all_heading / all_intro supply both. Keep them in sync with
    the matching override in layout/theme.liquid, which feeds <title> and
    the meta/OG tags for the same page.
  endcomment
  if template.name == 'collection'
    if collection.handle == 'all'
      if sub_heading == blank
        assign sub_heading = section.settings.all_heading
      endif
      if sub_intro == blank
        assign sub_intro = section.settings.all_intro
      endif
    elsif sub_intro == blank and collection.description != blank
      assign sub_intro = collection.description | remove: '<p>' | remove: '</p>' | strip
    endif
  endif
-%}

<section class="halora-subhero color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }}">
  {%- if section.settings.show_crumbs -%}
    <p class="halora-subhero__crumbs">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      {%- if section.settings.parent_label != blank -%}<a href="{{ section.settings.parent_url }}">{{ section.settings.parent_label }}</a><span class="sep">/</span>{%- endif -%}
      <span>{{ section.settings.crumb_current | default: display_title }}</span>
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if sub_heading != blank -%}
    <h1>{{ sub_heading }}</h1>
  {%- else -%}
    <h1>{{ display_title }}</h1>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if sub_intro != blank -%}<p>{{ sub_intro }}</p>{%- endif -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Halora subhero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section-halora-subhero",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_crumbs", "label": "Show breadcrumbs", "default": false },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_current", "label": "Current crumb label" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "parent_label", "label": "Parent crumb label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "parent_url", "label": "Parent crumb URL" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Catch-all collection (/collections/all)" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Shopify's /collections/all route has no record in the admin, so its heading and intro are set here. Other collections use their own Description automatically." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "all_heading", "label": "Heading for /collections/all" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "all_intro", "label": "Intro for /collections/all" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Halora subhero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
